QuestGuidance.Register("en",186,{
[5921]="700571F0\n1\tPick apples (total: 10)\tApple trees can be found in Lyndelby. You should pick apples for Ogiva Túcca.\n2\tDeliver the apples to the market\tYou should deliver the apples to the market in Lyndelby.\n3\tTalk to Ogiva Túcca in Lyndelby\tOgiva Túcca can be found in Lyndelby. You should talk to Ogiva Túcca.\n",
[5922]="700571DF\n1\tCheck fish traps (total: 8)\030Gather fish (total: 8)\030Gather worms for bait (total: 10)\tBait to gather can be found in Lyndelby. You should gather bait for Ubbo Bolga.\n2\tPlace the fish in the fish bucket\030Place the worms in the bait bucket\tBait buckets can be found in Lyndelby. You should deliver the bait to Ubbo Bolga.\n3\tTalk to Ubbo Bolga in Lyndelby\tUbbo Bolga can be found in Lyndelby. You should talk to Ubbo Bolga.\n",
[5923]="700571E8\n1\tCollect the picnic basket\030Gather up the picnic blanket\tThe picnic basket and blanket can both be found in Lyndelby. You should gather up the picnic items so that you can go on a picnic with Valaric Túcca.\n2\tFind an adequate place for a picnic\tAn adequate picnic spot can be found in Lyndelby. You should journey to the picnic spot.\n3\tPlace the picnic blanket\tAn adequate picnic spot can be found in Lyndelby. You should set down the picnic supplies.\n4\tUnpack the picnic basket\tAn adequate picnic spot can be found in Lyndelby. You should set down the picnic supplies.\n5\tTalk to Valaric Túcca on the picnic\tValaric Túcca can be found at the picnic spot in Lyndelby. You should talk to Valaric Túcca.\n6\tYes, you agree\030No, you do not agree\tValaric Túcca can be found at the picnic spot in Lyndelby. You should answer Valaric Túcca's question.\n7\tTalk to Valaric Túcca at the picnic spot\tValaric Túcca can be found at the picnic spot in Lyndelby. You should talk to Valaric Túcca.\n8\tYes, you agree\030No, you do not agree\tValaric Túcca can be found at the picnic spot in Lyndelby. You should answer Valaric Túcca's question.\n9\tTalk to Valaric Túcca at the picnic spot\tValaric Túcca can be found at the picnic spot in Lyndelby. You should talk to Valaric Túcca.\n10\tYes, you agree\030No, you do not agree\tValaric Túcca can be found at the picnic spot in Lyndelby. You should answer Valaric Túcca's question.\n11\tTalk to Valaric Túcca at the picnic\tValaric Túcca can be found at the picnic spot in Lyndelby. You should talk to Valaric Túcca.\n",
[5924]="700571E5\n1\tBoot pesky mountain-shrews off the fields (total: 8)\tPesky mountain-shrews can be found in Lyndelby. You should defeat the shrews for Vilihad Túcca.\n2\tTalk to Vilihad Túcca in Lyndelby\tVilihad Túcca can be found in Lyndelby. You should talk to Vilihad Túcca.\n",
[5925]="7004E90E\n1\tGather pine nuts (total: 12)\030Gather wild berries (total: 12)\tNuts and berries can be found in eastern Ered Mithrin near Erebor. You should collect pine nuts and wild berries.\n2\tBring the nuts and berries to Rúzat at Dôm Goru\tYou should bring the nuts and berries to Rúzat at Dôm Goru in Ered Mithrin.\n",
[5926]="7005109E\n1\tTalk to JWBarry\tBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete the discovery deeds for Glimmerdeep, Stormwall, and Thikil-gundu (the Steel Keep).\n",
[5927]="70058CF6\n1\tThe Greylin runs south out of Ered Mithrin to the east of Khadâsh-gâra. Gaustaf has asked you to pan the Greylin in several locations and bring him what you find. You should pan the Greylin.\t\n2\tDeliver the gem-stones and pebbles to Gaustaf\tGaustaf can be found at Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade. You have found a few small gem-stones and interesting pebbles from panning the Greylin. You should return to Gaustaf.\n",
[5928]="7000EC2B\n1\tBurn the tents of the Angmarim (total: 5)\tThe Angmarim tents are at the encampment south and east of Sûri-kylä, near the Forodwaith Pass. Pasi has asked you to return to the Angmarim encampment and burn down their tents with the kindling he gave you.\n2\tTalk to Pasi\030Collect Sytyke (Kindling)\tPasi is at Sûri-kyla, north and west of the Angmarim encampment. You should bring news of your success to Pasi.\n",
[5929]="70040389\n1\tDestroy Rashat-hai banners (total: 6)\tRashat-hai banners can be found throughout Tingobel in north-eastern Blackroot Vale. You have discovered banners of the Rashat-hai while exploring Tingobel and should destroy them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many Rashat-hai banners.\n",
[5930]="70022B2C\n1\tDefeat Grim Tomb-wights (total: 12)\tGrim Tomb-wights can be found within the Maze Wing of the Great Barrow.\n",
[5931]="70000613\n1\tReturn to Radagast with Grimbark's Seeds\030Collect Grimbark's Seeds\tGrimbark can be found at Garth Agarwen in the north of Agamaur, in the Lone-lands. Radagast is at Barad Dhorn, in the Eglan-camp. Radagast has asked you to bring him acorns from Grimbark's branches, so that he may plant them in the Old Forest, reclaiming some small part of the kinswoman's domain.\n",
[5932]="70041397\n1\tComplete 'Articles of Resilience'\030Complete 'Implements of Ferocity'\tYour brother Sterkist is at the Spire of Meeting, in Rivendell.\n2\tTalk to Sterkist in Rivendell\tYour brother Sterkist is at the Spire of Meeting, in Rivendell.\n3\tTalk to Grimbeorn at Vindurhal, in the Misty Mountains\tGrimbeorn has come to the High Pass, in the Misty Mountains. He is at the camp called Vindurhal, in the narrow space between Eastern Bruinen Source and North High Pass. Sterkist has told you that Grimbeorn planned to travel into the High Pass if you completed the tasks set before you.\n4\tTalk to Sterkist in Rivendell\tYour brother Sterkist is by the Spire of Meeting, in Rivendell.\n",
[5933]="70037984\n1\tElgyth's belongings can be found in her home, and among them may be a letter telling of Grimbold's news from the Fords of Isen. You should search Elgyth's home for the latest news of Grimbold.\t\n2\tTake your leave of Elgyth\tElgyth is in her home in Grimslade, in the south-eastern Westfold. You should take your leave of Elgyth.\n",
[5934]="70016B1F\n1\tDefeat fiery grims in the Flaming Deeps (total: 8)\tFiery grims can be found throughout the Flaming Deeps. You should extinguish the Fiery Grims, for the dwarves do not love them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have extinguished the bright, roaming flames of the Fiery Grims that prowl the Flaming Deeps. The dwarves will rest easier knowing that their number is lessened.\n",
[5935]="70037C82\n1\tHelp save Grimslade from the half-orc attack\tHildith is in the Mead Hall at Grimslade. You should speak with Hildith.\n2\tSpeak with Hildith\tHildith is in the Mead Hall at Grimslade. You should speak with Hildith.\n",
[5936]="7000AE58\n1\tTalk to Tordúr at Glân Vraig\tTravel east and south from the Grimwood Lumber Camp to inform Captain-General Tordúr that the Grimwood Lumber Camp belongs to the Free People. You have been tasked with informing the Captain-General that the battle at the Grimwood is won.\n",
[5937]="70009EF6\n1\tDefeat Free Peoples at the Grimwood Lumber-camp (total: 6)\tFight Angmar's foes within the bounds of the Grimwood Lumber-camp. You were instructed to stand this ground and fight for the glory of Angmar in defence of the Grimwood Lumber-camp.\n2\tTalk to Chieftain Torbok\030Talk to War-tyrant Akúlhun\tIf Torbok is defeated or the lumber camp has fallen to the Free Peoples, return to Gramsfoot and face the wrath of War-tyrant Akúlhun. You should return to Chieftain Torbok at the Grimwood Lumber Camp to gloat of your victories against the Free Peoples.\n",
[5938]="70048F7A\n1\tDefeat Gristlebite\tGristlebite can be found patrolling Mordor. You have encountered the threatening Gristlebite. Roaming the noxious valley of Lhingris, the beast patrols with her brood.\n2\tDefeat Gristlebite\tGristlebite can be found patrolling Mordor. You have encountered the threatening Gristlebite. Roaming the noxious valley of Lhingris, the beast patrols with her brood.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Gristlebite.\n",
[5939]="7002D452\n1\tTalk to Grobo Dogwort\tGrobo Dogwort has a hobbit-hole in Staddle. Grobo Dogwort's nephew is keeping a bag of turtles in his uncle's shed, and you should ask Grobo Dogwort if you can collect them.\n2\tPick up the turtle-carrying sack in Grobo Dogwort's shed\tThe turtle-carrying sack is somewhere inside Grobo Dogwort's shed, a hobbit-hole adjacent to his home. Grobo Dogwort is terrified of turtles and wants you to put the ones loose in his shed back in the sack in which his nephew was keeping them.\n3\tSave Grobo Dogwort's peace of mind by gathering up turtles from his shed (total: 8)\tTurtles can be found all throughout Grobo Dogwort's shed. Grobo Dogwort is terrified of turtles and wants you to collect all of the creatures that escaped from the poorly-tied sack his nephew left in Grobo's shed.\n4\tShow the turtle-carrying sack to Grobo Dogwort in his hobbit-hole\tGrobo Dogwort is in his hobbit-hole, adjacent to the turtle-filled shed, on the eastern side of Staddle. You have gathered up the turtles that plagued Grobo Dogwort and should speak to him now that they are safely ensconced once again in the turtle-carrying sack.\n",
[5940]="70032BE3\n1\tClaw Hollow, The Chittering Hole, and The Great Hive have untapped deposits which seem to attract the gredbyg. The gredbyg have grown out of control in the south of the Redhorn Lodes. Their hive is enormous, and was built upon many untapped deposits of ore. It is likely this tunnel could be the best location for mithril prospecting in all of Moria!\t\n2\tReturn to Kúli\tKúli and Auti are camped on the northern edge of the enormous grodbog hive. Kúli is interested in determining good mining locations within the hive. He is hoping that some day the grodbog hive won't be as dangerous, and that mining those places will be possible.\n",
[5941]="700169BE\n1\tDefeat gredbyg in Nud-heden (total: 10)\tGredbyg can be found within Nud-heden, in the Chittering Hole, south-east of the Orc-watch. Auti wants you to slay the gredbyg who are nursing their young.\n2\tTalk to Auti at the Orc-watch\tAuti is at the Orc-watch, north-west of Nud-heden. Auti will be pleased to hear that the gredbyg have been defeated and are no longer nursing their young.\n",
[5942]="70032C27\n1\tDefeat gredbyg in Nud-heden (total: 10)\tGredbyg can be found within Nud-heden, found inside the grodbog hive, south of where Kúli and Auti are camped. You should defeat the gredbyg at Nud-heden.\n2\tReturn to Auti\tAuti is camped with Kúli, just north of the grodbog hive. Auti will be pleased to hear that the gredbyg have been defeated and Nud-heden is another step closer to again being a home of dwarves.\n",
[5943]="700561DE\n1\tGroom horses (total: 6)\tHorses can be found in the throughout the Kingstead neighbourhoods. You should groom some horses.\n",
[5944]="70071868\n1\tCleanse monstrous fungi (total: 8)\tSílivat has given you enchanted water that he hopes will cleanse the fungi growing on the eastern edges of Sul Madásh and prevent them from spreading the blight deeper into the settlement.\n2\tReturn to Sílivat\tReturn to Sílivat and inform him that you have cleansed the monstrous fungi found in Sul Madásh.\n",
[5945]="70032BDF\n1\tDestroy fungal mushrooms (total: 6)\tThe eastern edge of the Redhorn Lodes is infested with an aggressively growing fungus.\n2\tReturn to Knakk\tKnakk is camped on the elevated walkway in the north-east corner of the Redhorn Lodes.\n",
[5946]="70057F3F\n1\tWater bushes (total: 4)\030Pull out weeds (total: 5)\tThe garden lies on the Third Circle of Minas Tirith, to the north-west of the entryway between the Second and Third Circles. The statue of Steward Egalmoth keeps watch over the garden. Lebadar has asked you to pull out the weeds and water the bushes there.\n2\tReturn to Lebadar\tLebadar waits for you on the Second Circle, at the base of the entrance to the Third. You should assure him that the garden has been tended.\n",
[5947]="7003E459\n1\tGather seed-pods from the forest floor (total: 12)\tSeed-pods can be found throughout central Fangorn Forest. Quickbeam's Huorn has begun stowing away seed-pods to plant as you travel. You should aid in collecting them.\n2\tGive the seed-pods to Quickbeam's Huorn\tQuickbeam's Huorn can be found at your side or can be called with your whistle. You have gathered many seed-pods from the forest floor and should now give them to Quickbeam's Huorn.\n",
[5948]="7000E4DE\n1\tEarn the trust of Kaj\030Earn the trust of Niko\030Earn the trust of Lauri\tOra's son Kaj may be found near her, at the main lodge. Ora's best scout, Lauri, is near the southern gate of Pynti-peldot. Ora's Master of the Hunt, Niko, may be found at his camp, south-west along the road. Ora told you that you must gain her trust by helping other Lossoth of her tribe. She suggested you start with her son Kaj, the scout Lauri, and Niko, her Master of the Hunt.\n2\tTalk to Chief Ora\tOra is at Pynti-peldot. Having gained the trust of three of the Lossoth, you should return at once to Ora.\n",
[5949]="70045FE9\n1\tPick up an unfilled barrel\tYou should pick up an unfilled barrel so that you can collect any scattered remains found on the outer walls in Minas Tirith.\n2\tCollect scattered remains (total: 10)\tYou should use the unfilled barrel to collect any scattered remains that you can find on the outer walls of Minas Tirith.\n3\tDeliver the filled barrel to Húrin\tHúrin can be found outside the front gates of Minas Tirith. You should deliver the filled barrel to Húrin.\n",
[5950]="7005784F\n1\tFind Grugáth\tGrugáth and his kin have already laid waste to several villages in Misthallow in this way, and now they stand empty. He must be destroyed before he can be once again unleashed.\n2\tDefeat Grugáth in Grazadh-gropor\tGrugáth, leader of the wood-trolls that lurk within Grazadh-gropor, resents all intrusions to his lair. Grugáth and his kin have already laid waste to several villages in Misthallow in this way, and now they stand empty. He must be destroyed before he bring any more harm.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[5951]="70008878\n1\tReturn to Quartermaster Apsduf at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect norbog-gizzards (total: 5)\030Collect slabs of norbog-meat (total: 5)\tNerbyg can be found along the banks of the Hoardale River surrounding Tol Ascarnen. Collect the gizzards and meat from the nerbyg to give to Apsduf for your nightly gruel.\n",
[5952]="70040EC0\n1\tDissenters of Lothíriel's rule can be found in the Court of the Fount. You should disperse the dissenters.\t\n2\tCompleted\tYou have ushered away a number of dissenters in the Court of the Fount, restoring order to the bustling square.\n",
})
